 <Worksheet ss:Name="GPIO_TestPlan">
  <Table ss:DefaultColumnWidth="120">
   <Column ss:Index="1" ss:Width="40"/>
   <Column ss:Index="2" ss:Width="80"/>
   <Column ss:Index="3" ss:Width="110"/>
   <Column ss:Index="4" ss:Width="200"/>
   <Column ss:Index="5" ss:Width="350"/>
   <Column ss:Index="6" ss:Width="200"/>
   <Column ss:Index="7" ss:Width="450"/>
   <Column ss:Index="8" ss:Width="400"/>
   <Column ss:Index="9" ss:Width="70"/>
   <Column ss:Index="10" ss:Width="140"/>
   <Column ss:Index="11" ss:Width="140"/>
   <Column ss:Index="12" ss:Width="300"/>
   <Column ss:Index="13" ss:Width="280"/>
   <Column ss:Index="14" ss:Width="160"/>
   <Row ss:Height="30">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">S.No</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">IP_NAME</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Case ID</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Case Name</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Description</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Preconditions</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Steps</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Expected Results</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Priority</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Category</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Test Type</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Registers Tested</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Source Folder</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Header"><Data ss:Type="String">Source Files</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:Height="180">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="Number">1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO_TC_001</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">gpio_reg_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">Validates GPIO register reset values and verifies read/write functionality across defined registers using multiple data patterns and masks.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Initialize the test and enumerate all GPIO registers defined for validation.&#10;2. For each defined GPIO register, read the value and compare it against its expected reset value.&#10;3. For each register, apply a set of predefined data patterns (e.g., 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000) respecting the register's write mask, then write the value.&#10;4. Read back the register value and verify it against the expected value considering the register's read mask.&#10;5. Repeat the write/read verification for all patterns across all defined registers.&#10;6. Aggregate results and report pass if all comparisons match; otherwise report fail.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">1. All GPIO registers match their documented reset values.&#10;2. All masked write operations are accepted correctly and preserved by subsequent reads.&#10;3. All readbacks match the expected values across all data patterns and registers.&#10;4. Overall test status reports PASS when all verifications succeed; otherwise FAIL.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">Register Validation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GP0_GPIO_8, GP0_GPIO_9, GP0_GPIO_10, GP0_GPIO_11, GP0_GPIO_12, GP0_GPIO_13, GP0_GPIO_14, GP0_GPIO_15, GP0_GPIO_16, GP0_GPIO_17, GP0_GPIO_18, GP0_GPIO_19, GP0_GPIO_20, GP0_GPIO_21, GP0_GPIO_22, GP0_GPIO_23, GP0_GPIO_24, GP0_GPIO_25, GP0_GPIO_26, GP0_GPIO_27</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">TestRepo/gpio/gpio_reg_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">program.c, test_define.c</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:Height="220">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="Number">2</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO_TC_002</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">test_gpio_negedge_intr_en</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">Validates GPIO negative-edge interrupt detection and handling for all 32 GPIO pads. Configures each pad for negedge interrupt, drives a falling-edge signal transition, verifies interrupt is raised via ISR, checks interrupt status register, clears the interrupt, and confirms the status is cleared.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Enable GIC IRQ for GPIO (IRQ 87 for GPIO0 or IRQ 88 for GPIO1).&#10;2. Enable GPIO interrupt in the system register (LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1).&#10;3. Drive all GPIO output pads high (write 0xFFFFFFFF to pad output register 0xA0243ffc).&#10;4. Configure all 32 GPIO pads (GP0_GPIO_8 to GP0_GPIO_39) for negative-edge interrupt detection by setting bits [20], [18], [16].&#10;5. For each pad (i = 0 to 31): clear raw interrupt status (GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1), enable per-pad interrupt (GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1), set int_pend flag, drive pad output high then low to create a falling edge.&#10;6. Wait for ISR (Default_IRQHandler) to fire with a timeout of 5000 iterations.&#10;7. In ISR: verify pad input value is low (bit[0] == 0), verify interrupt status bit is set in GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, clear the interrupt by resetting negedge enable, write to GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, verify status register is cleared to 0x0, clear sysreg status and GIC IRQ.&#10;8. Report PASS if all 32 pads complete without errors; otherwise report FAIL.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">1. GIC IRQ is enabled successfully for the GPIO instance.&#10;2. Each GPIO pad correctly detects a negative-edge (falling) signal transition.&#10;3. ISR (Default_IRQHandler) is triggered within the timeout period for each pad.&#10;4. Pad input value reads as low (bit[0] == 0) after the falling edge.&#10;5. Interrupt status bit is correctly set in GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 for the active pad.&#10;6. Interrupt is successfully cleared — GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 reads 0x0 after clearing.&#10;7. System register status and GIC IRQ are cleared without errors.&#10;8. Overall test reports PASS (test_err == 0) when all 32 pads pass; otherwise FAIL.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">Interrupt Validation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GP0_GPIO_8 to GP0_GPIO_27 (pad config), GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, GPIO_INTR_RAW_STCLR1, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_negedge_intr_en</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">program.c, test_define.c</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
   <Row ss:Height="220">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="Number">3</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO_TC_003</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">Validates GPIO positive-edge interrupt detection and handling for all 32 GPIO pads simultaneously. Configures all pads for posedge interrupt, sets IO control groups for input mode, enables group interrupts, drives a rising-edge signal transition on all pads, verifies group interrupt is raised via ISR, clears all per-pin interrupts, and confirms group status is cleared.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Enable GIC IRQ for GPIO (IRQ 87 for GPIO0 or IRQ 88 for GPIO1).&#10;2. Enable GPIO interrupt in the system register (LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1).&#10;3. Configure all 32 GPIO pads (GP0_GPIO_8 to GP0_GPIO_39) for positive-edge interrupt detection by writing 0x00020000 (bit17=posedge_en).&#10;4. Set IO control groups 1-4 for input mode (write 0x000000FF to GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1 through GROUP4).&#10;5. Enable all group interrupts by writing 0xFFFFFFFF to GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1.&#10;6. For each pad (i = 0 to 31): drive all pads low (write 0x00000000), set int_pend flag, drive all pads high (write 0xFFFFFFFF) to create a rising edge.&#10;7. Wait for ISR (Default_IRQHandler) to fire with a timeout of 2000 iterations.&#10;8. In ISR: read group interrupt status (GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1), verify it is non-zero, mask group interrupts during service, clear all per-pin raw status by writing bit16 (iclr) to each pad register, verify group interrupt status is cleared to 0x0, clear sysreg status and GIC IRQ, re-enable group interrupts.&#10;9. Drive pads low again to prepare for next iteration.&#10;10. Report PASS if all 32 iterations complete without errors; otherwise report FAIL.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">1. GIC IRQ is enabled successfully for the GPIO instance.&#10;2. All 32 GPIO pads correctly detect a positive-edge (rising) signal transition.&#10;3. ISR (Default_IRQHandler) is triggered within the timeout period for each iteration.&#10;4. Group interrupt status (GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1) is non-zero confirming group interrupt was raised.&#10;5. All per-pin interrupts are successfully cleared — GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1 reads 0x0 after clearing all 32 pins.&#10;6. System register status (LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1) is cleared without errors.&#10;7. GIC IRQ is cleared and group interrupts are re-enabled for the next iteration.&#10;8. Overall test reports PASS (test_err == 0) when all 32 iterations pass; otherwise FAIL.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">Interrupt Validation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">NA</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GP0_GPIO_8 to GP0_GPIO_27 (pad config), GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1, GP0_INTR1_INTR_STS1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP1, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP2, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP3, GPIO_IO_CTRL_GROUP4, LSS_SYSREG_INTR_EN1, LSS_SYSREG_RAW_STCR1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_pedge_all_pads_en</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">program.c, test_define.c</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
  </Table>
 </Worksheet>
